            "chunk_type": "isnad",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "Sahl ibn Ziyad, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from al-Nawfali, from al-Husayn ibn al-Mukhtar, from a man, who said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 16,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "arabic_text": "قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ إِنِّي رَجُلٌ مُؤَذِّنٌ فَإِذَا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْغَيْمِ لَمْ أَعْرِفِ الْوَقْتَ، قَالَ: «إِذَا صَاحَ الدِّيكُ ثَلَاثَةَ أَصْوَاتٍ وِلَاءً فَقَدْ زَالَتِ الشَّمْسُ وَدَخَلَ وَقْتُ الصَّلَاةِ»",
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "I said to Abi Abdillah عليه السلام: I am a man who calls the adhan, and when it is a cloudy day I do not know the time. He said: “When the rooster crows three calls in succession, then the sun has declined and the time of salat (prayer) has entered.”",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 45,
            "word_start": 16
          }
        ],
